 # dryer
+
+Svelte (`.svelte`) files are analyzed as TypeScript script blocks. Both module
+and instance scripts retain their original source lines and UTF-8 byte offsets.
+Markup, styles, and template expressions are excluded. The extraction helper is
+also used by crapper and mutator; dryer keeps its own copy to remain standalone.

 dryer finds candidate duplicate code in Clojure, Java, Go, TypeScript, Rust, and Python. One run detects the language of each source file, normalizes that language's forms, and reports pairs whose structure is close enough to review.

